// bao1x.repl -- Renode platform for the REAL Baochip-1x SoC.
//
// Generated from the real baochip/baochip-1x SVD (rtl/scripts/headergen/
// output/bao1x_peri.svd, fetched live -- see renode/bao1x_peri.svd for
// the exact copy used, with two real, documented compatibility fixes
// applied for svd2repl's parser -- see renode/README.md for details)
// via xous-core's own svd2repl tool (svd2repl/src/main.rs), NOT the
// existing Precursor-only xous-core Renode support
// (emulation/soc/betrusted-soc.repl, utralib/renode/renode.svd --
// dated 2022-06-11, models Precursor addresses like 0xf0000000, nothing
// matching Baochip-1x's real addresses).
//
// Per baoregon-trail issue #2's explicit scope: covers real SoC
// peripherals only (GPIO/IOX for buttons, DUART for console -- SPI/
// UDMA_SPIM for the real memory-LCD display protocol left as a
// generic catch-all region for now, see the "udma" region below and
// README.md's "Known limitations" section). Deliberately excludes any
// BIO-coprocessor behavioral modeling -- that's already covered at much
// higher fidelity by the existing bio-sim Verilator RTL simulator
// (see NEXT_STEPS.md's bio-sim real-world check). WiFi/Bluetooth are
// NOT modeled because they are not real Baochip-1x SoC peripherals at
// all (confirmed zero hits in Xous's own generated hardware header,
// betrusted-io/xous-core/utralib/src/generated/bao1x.rs) -- if the
// physical badge has WiFi/BT, it's a separate board-level chip, out of
// scope for a SoC platform description.
//
// Real, plentiful "// Unrecognized peripheral" stubs below are EXPECTED
// and NORMAL -- this matches the existing Precursor .repl's own pattern
// exactly (most real peripherals don't have a corresponding Renode C#
// model yet; they still get their memory correctly mapped as inert
// MappedMemory below, which is enough to catch real address-collision
// bugs like the one this exact platform's memory-map fix
// (commit 144dd81, docs/baochip-1x-memory-map-findings.md) resolved).

// Renode Platform file generated by svd2repl
// This file is automatically generated
cpu: CPU.VexRiscv @ sysbus
    cpuType: "rv32imac_zicsr_zifencei"
    PerformanceInMips: 120
